import json
from pathlib import Path
p=json.loads(Path('documentation_revision/paragraphs.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
changes=[]
def para(i,text):
    changes.append({'find':p[i].strip(),'replacement':text,'expected':sum(t.count(p[i].strip()) for t in p)})
def exact(old,new):
    before='\n'.join(p)
    a=before.index('Appendix A',before.index('References',5000)) if False else 0
    changes.append({'find':old,'replacement':new,'expected':before.count(old)})
para(197,'This study covers the design, development, and pilot evaluation of BARANGAYAN for Barangay Ampid I, San Mateo, Rizal. It provides a resident Android application, a resident website, and a staff and administrator website using React Native, Expo, Next.js, and Supabase. Its main contribution combines flood-weighted Dijkstra evacuation routing with a separate Open-Meteo rainfall advisory. Supporting modules cover profiles, document requests, payments, incident reports, medical drives, announcements, and administration. Features are accepted only after the specified tests pass; prototype screens alone do not establish completion.')
para(200,'Residents view document requirements, fees, and processing targets; submit applications; and track pickup status. Profile records use separate first-name and last-name fields. Residents submit identification and proof of residency for authorized staff review; GPS is a preliminary check only. Household records identify one designated household head for coordination. Relationship choices depend on the selected member, and duplicate spouse links for the same person are rejected. These rules remain subject to functional verification.')
para(202,'Residents track document requests, incident reports, and health registrations through their approved status stages. Processing targets identify overdue requests. Status changes must appear in the resident and staff interfaces without a manual page refresh; this behavior is verified through integration tests.')
para(204,'Residents submit an incident category, description, location, and supporting photos. Leaflet displays OpenStreetMap data with attribution. Upload validation checks supported image formats, file size, and readability; authorized staff review relevance. Image upload does not imply automated image recognition. Blocked-road reports retain their source, time, and verification status for DRRM review.')
para(206,'The emergency module provides preparedness guides, hotlines, evacuation-center information, announcements, and family check-in. Announcements require start and end dates and may include a banner; expired items move to archives. Emergency notifications should play sound when notification permissions and device settings allow it. QR check-in must validate the code, selected family members, center, and attendance record, with clear invalid-code and duplicate-scan responses. Offline access is limited to previously stored guides and contacts; scanning and attendance updates require verification under the supported network conditions.')
para(207,'The rainfall advisory requests hourly model-estimated precipitation for Ampid I. It compares the latest completed hour (R1) and the heaviest forecast hour of the next three hours (F3) with configurable application thresholds of 7.5, 15, and 30 mm. These thresholds are informed by PAGASA rainfall-intensity classes; the app does not issue official PAGASA warnings. Stale or unavailable readings are labelled clearly. The advisory is displayed beside the route and does not change its weights.')
para(209,'Dijkstra selects the available evacuation center with the lowest flood-weighted route cost for walking, motorcycle or tricycle, or car. Recorded flood depths, published closures, blocked-road marks, and center availability determine usable segments. Distances and walking estimates are shown with alternative routes. Route recalculation after changed conditions must be tested separately from automatic destination switching; the resident retains the selected destination. The route is guidance based on recorded conditions, not a guarantee of safety.')
para(212,'Registration. Residents review the drive schedule, eligibility requirements, and available slots before applying for themselves or an eligible family member. The application records the selected applicant and returns a reference number. Any priority or waitlist rule must be approved by the responsible health staff and verified before use.')
para(213,'Status tracking. Residents view their registration status and history. Duplicate applications and conflicting records are checked against the approved drive rules.')
para(215,'Residents choose pay at pickup or QR Ph through PayMongo. Participating banks and e-wallets may pay the generated QR code. The request status changes only after a verified payment confirmation. Development and pilot payments remain in sandbox mode; live settlement is outside the evaluated scope.')
para(216,'STAFF AND ADMINISTRATOR WEBSITE')
para(218,'Authorized staff view pending requests, ready-for-pickup documents, collections, registered residents, and incident summaries. Document staff review applications and residency evidence, update status, and preview the approved document before printing. Treasurer-assigned staff review transactions. Changes must update the displayed records without a manual refresh.')
para(220,'Role-based access limits each account to its assigned records and actions. Privileged operations use server-side functions and database policies. Authorized staff may register residents and send account invitations; delivery and activation require testing. Privacy controls support data access and deletion requests, but legal compliance also requires approved notices, retention rules, consent procedures, and staff accountability (Republic Act No. 10173, 2012).')
para(227,'Drive creation. Authorized health staff set the category, date, start and end times, venue, eligibility, and capacity. The system must reject a same-category event that conflicts with an existing date and time slot.')
para(228,'Registration monitoring. Authorized health staff review applicants, eligibility, available slots, and application status.')
para(229,'Attendance and stock. Attendance and stock adjustments require authorized confirmation and test evidence; a displayed QR code alone does not confirm dispensing.')
para(230,'Waitlist and no-show handling. Any slot-release or waitlist process follows the approved health-office rule and is verified before being described as automatic.')
para(232,'Residents access published FAQs and barangay contact details. Assigned content staff maintain this information through the website.')
para(234,'Staff update approved request stages, including rejection, processing, ready for pickup, and completion. Residents still collect physical documents at the barangay. An integration test verifies that both interfaces display the same saved status without manual refresh.')
para(236,'Expired announcements move to archives and leave active lists. Authorized staff may view and restore archived records, subject to retention rules. Archiving is distinct from permanent deletion, and restored announcements must satisfy valid publication dates.')
para(239,'Routing is limited to the mapped Ampid I network and the approved transport modes. Recorded depths are historical inputs, not live street measurements. A missing depth is unknown; the current zero fallback must not be presented as a confirmed dry road. Routes using incomplete data require a visible limitation and DRRM review. No verified elevation model is assumed. Synthetic networks and depths test the algorithm; they do not establish local flood accuracy. Walking times use fixed speeds and exclude changes caused by rain, crowding, or floodwater.')
para(240,'The advisory uses model-estimated rainfall and does not predict street flood depth or river stage. Its thresholds require DRRM review and do not replace official warnings. Network access is required for current weather, transactions, notifications, and shared updates. Only stored guides and contacts may be read offline. The routing design excludes turn-by-turn voice navigation, live tracking, and automatic destination switching; recalculation behavior must match its test record. Android is the evaluated mobile platform. Pilot evaluation covers one partner barangay and does not establish performance elsewhere.')
para(526,'Open-Meteo is selected because its hourly precipitation, explicit model selection, and historical datasets support the project’s advisory and controlled tests without a free-tier API key. OpenWeather and WeatherAPI also provide weather services, but require API-key management; their inclusion here is a design comparison, not an accuracy ranking (Open-Meteo, n.d.; OpenWeather, n.d.; WeatherAPI.com, n.d.). A scheduled server function requests one fixed barangay location. Data are model estimates, not rain-gauge observations, river-stage readings, or street-flood measurements. The free service has no uptime guarantee; stale or failed requests must display an unavailable-data message. Table 7 identifies the variables used.')
para(552,'The function requests an update every 60 minutes. Failed, timed-out, missing, negative, or implausible readings are rejected rather than stored as zero. The last accepted reading retains its timestamp; after three hours it is labelled stale. The advisory links residents to official PAGASA information while routes continue to use recorded road conditions (Open-Meteo, n.d.).')
para(736,'Routing inputs are the road graph, recorded flood depths, approved closures, blocked-road marks, and center availability. Open-Meteo rainfall is a separate advisory input. Historical rainfall supports test preparation only. A local geographic layer must retain its source, issue date, scale, licence, and DRRM review status.')
para(737,'Forms and server functions validate inputs before storage. For flood reports, the required record fields are report ID, reporter role, road-segment ID, coordinates, reported time, depth in metres or unknown, evidence, verification status, reviewer, review time, valid-until time, and closure status. Unknown depth is stored distinctly from measured zero. Access and retention follow the assigned role and approved policy.')
para(745,'Flood-data flow: resident or field staff report → DRRM verification → approved road-segment update → shared conditions → Dijkstra recalculation. Unverified reports remain labelled and must not be described as confirmed flood depth. DRRM reviews closures and expiry times before clearing a restriction.')
para(836,'Figure 2.2 is read with the flood-data flow above. The deployment design uses separate Next.js resident and staff websites on Vercel, a hosted Supabase database, authentication, storage and server functions, and an Android APK distributed for pilot use. Actual deployment URLs and release versions are recorded during verification. Current transactions, weather, maps, and synchronized updates require internet access; cached guides are the limited offline exception.')
para(883,'The study uses developmental research to design, implement, and evaluate BARANGAYAN. Functional tests assess specified workflows; task-based evaluation measures usability for the assigned user groups. Planned functions, implemented features, and passed tests are reported separately.')
para(939,'Rainfall, flood, and road records. Residents or authorized field staff submit geolocated reports through the incident form or an approved DRRM reporting channel. DRRM checks the location and evidence, confirms the depth or closure, and records the reviewer, time, and expiry before publishing a road update. Historical susceptibility is checked against government hazard information through HazardHunterPH and DRRM records (Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology [PHIVOLCS], n.d.). A verified Ampid I map must distinguish mapped hazard classes and relative elevation; no street classification or elevation value is assumed before this review. Susceptibility provides context; verified segment depth and closure rules determine the implemented route weights.')
para(940,'Routing tests use synthetic networks with known distances, depths, closures, and center status. Tests cover changed conditions, unknown depths, unavailable centers, and no-route cases. Hand calculations verify route cost. Results establish software correctness only; local geographic accuracy requires separate DRRM validation.')
para(1013,'Table 12 summarizes the platform scope. Resident Android and web accounts access their own profiles, requests, reports, payments, health registrations, and emergency information. Staff use the website for assigned workflows; administrators manage configuration and access. Equivalent resident services share records across platforms, while camera, notification, and offline behavior are tested separately.')
para(1055,'Platform and permitted actions')
para(1058,'Android and resident web: manage own profile, household, requests, incidents, payments, registrations, and privacy requests; no staff administration')
para(1061,'Staff web: review authorized summaries and oversight information; changes require an assigned operational permission')
para(1063,'Assigned staff and administrator')
para(1064,'Staff web permission matrix: Clerk/secretary—residency review, requests and print preview; health worker—drives and registrations; tanod/incident staff—incident review; treasurer—payment records; content staff—announcements and archives; administrator—accounts and configuration. Each assignment requires server and database enforcement; unassigned actions are denied.')
para(1067,'Staff web: verify flood reports; publish depths, closures and center availability; review advisory status; retain reviewer and expiry records')
para(1110,'Each requirement is linked to its platform, role, module, data fields, permission, and test ID. The SIA 2 list is treated as a dated defect baseline; a later screenshot or code change does not close a defect without a retest result. Payments remain in sandbox, and DRRM owns the approval of emergency content and local geographic data.')
para(1113,'The implementation uses React Native and Expo for Android, Next.js for the resident and staff websites, and Supabase for authentication, database policies, storage, real-time updates, and server functions. Vercel configuration is included for both websites. Verification records identify the deployed URL, build version, network conditions, and provider mode without exposing credentials. A hosted configuration is not proof of production readiness.')
para(1118,'Each test records its ID, platform, role, precondition, input, expected result, observed result, status, evidence, and corrective action. The SIA 2 acceptance checks below are requirements for retesting, not claims that defects are already resolved.')
para(1158,'Requirements traceability links each revision to a test and result. SIA 2 retesting must verify: QR scan validity and duplicate handling; separate name fields and relationship/spouse rules; announcement dates, banners and expiry; emergency sound under supported settings; conflicting event rejection; automatic request-status refresh; residency review; archive and restore; correct print preview; image format, size and relevance review; invitation delivery and activation; weather, map and network failures; and verified QR Ph or pay-at-pickup status. A defect closes only after the expected result is reproduced and evidence is recorded.')
para(1115,'Revision records identify the requirement, affected section, implemented change, test result, evidence, and remaining limitation. Completed, pending, provider-dependent, and excluded functions are labelled consistently. Appendix C records interface examples; it does not replace functional test evidence.')
para(1470,'Philippine Statistics Authority. (2025, July 17). 2024 Census of Population (POPCEN) population counts declared official by the President. https://psa.gov.ph/content/2024-census-population-popcen-population-counts-declared-official-president')
para(1471,'Piamonte, C. N., Curada, J. P. M., & Zaragoza, M. C. (2026). Project Bantay: Breadth-first search and Dijkstra implementation for community-accessible disaster response. In Proceedings of WCTP 2025 (Atlantis Highlights in Computer Sciences, Vol. 24, pp. 629–645). https://doi.org/10.2991/978-94-6239-638-8_33')
exact('This study is the first one to combine Dijkstra routing with the Open-Meteo Forecast and Historical Weather APIs in a single residential mobile application.','The contribution is the integration of flood-weighted routing and a separate rainfall advisory with resident services for Barangay Ampid I.')
exact('nearest available evacuation center','available evacuation center with the lowest flood-weighted route cost')
exact('latest observed hour','latest model-estimated hour')
exact('latest observed hourly rain','latest model-estimated hourly rain')
Path('documentation_revision/replacements.json').write_text(json.dumps(changes,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print(len(changes),'changes prepared')
